WEBVTT

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.160
You would always find me when I got lost.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.950
Misao!

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.680
I'm counting on you.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.680
Come find me.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.590
Wait, Misao!

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.200
Misao!

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.820
Misao!

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.430
"Squish?"

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.250
Nia, what are you doing here?

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.250
I could ask you the same thing.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.500
I thought it would be nice to wake you...

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.700
...but you ruined it by grabbing my chest...

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.730
...while calling another woman's name.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.110
Calm down, Nia.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.050
Shut up, you player!

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.450
<i>"Asura Cryin' 2"</i>

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.840
"Adjoined Death and Peace"

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.650
What happened to you?

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.680
Oh, uh...

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.000
It's his punishment for tarnishing a girl's purity.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.680
Oh, Takatsuki...

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.150
Could I get another...

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.080
I'll protect you, Takatsuki.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.430
Natsume-kun...

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:38.960
Here.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.600
Thanks.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.360
Natsume, did you do something to Kanade?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.660
W-what? I...

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.970
I'm sure he violated her...

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.850
...just like he violated me.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:50.820
Nia!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.230
How bold for a freeloader.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.110
But we can't let that go unpunished.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.370
Right, Toru?

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.520
Right, Aki-chan.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.360
You've got the wrong idea!

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.390
What a lousy morning.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.000
I confessed my feelings for Takatsuki...

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.640
Why isn't she acting any differently?

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.010
Takatsuki, I...

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:29.890
...like you.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.890
She heard me, right?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.230
I guess Takatsuki isn't ready yet.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.730
You really are Nia, right?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.110
Where did that come from?

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.810
You've really grown...

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.690
What are you looking at?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.280
T-that's not what I meant!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.980
Then what did you mean?

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.120
You really came here five years before me?

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.120
So?

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.440
It must have been tough on your own.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:08.200
My power makes life easy.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.280
You should consider yourself lucky.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.780
You're getting to see how beautiful I've become.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.680
Sorry to make you wait.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:19.830
Takatsuki.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.120
Why are you here, too?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.470
And looking like that...

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.790
It's my uniform.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.320
We're going to Rakurowa High School, right?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.230
Aki, keep an eye on Tomoharu.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.350
Understood.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.080
What about Nia and Takatsuki?

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.660
I've got business with Kanade.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.010
Right, Kanade?

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.160
Yes.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:40.830
But I need to talk to Takatsuki, too.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.480
Hey, wait!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.650
So, Kanade...

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.170
Aki-san, is it okay for you to be going to school?

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.850
Why would there be a problem?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.340
I was a student here.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.750
I don't think that's the issue...

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.130
Get out of the way!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.970
Ouch...

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:14.910
Are you okay?

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.580
Is there something on my face?

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:21.900
Aine...

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.750
You know me?

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.190
Yeah...

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.540
You might not know it...

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.270
...but I've known you for a long time.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.030
What is this? A confession of love?

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.970
Getting yourself into trouble again?

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:40.410
Shiro-kun.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.520
Reishiro.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.020
And Shuri-san.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.310
Didn't I tell you to let the vendors take care of it?

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.340
But it's for the party.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.420
As a member of the Cooking Club, I wanted to see the ingredients.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.210
Are you alright?

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:56.830
I'm fine.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.000
Those clothes...

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.440
It's the uniform of the student council vice president.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.730
You seem okay.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:04.930
Yes.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.400
Good bye, then.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:07.810
Shuri-san...

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.110
Natsume!

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.370
Saeki.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.420
What were you thinking?

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.250
You shouldn't be skipping class with permission.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.920
Oh, uh...

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:18.060
You'll be working like a dog today.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:18.830
What?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.180
Don't play dumb.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.440
We have to prepare for the Christmas party, remember?

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.260
Christmas party?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.140
Come on, let's go.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.790
I can't leave you or Higuchi alone for a second.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.340
You're always running away the second I turn my back.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:32.930
Good grief.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.010
Aki Kitsutaka-senpai.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.420
Yo.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.100
I guess Saeki and Higuchi are the same here.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.420
It's almost nostalgic...

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:04.650
Working hard?

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.530
Thanks.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.530
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.030
Since we've had the chance to talk.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.400
You quit the club...

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.020
...and skip class without permission.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.900
Is it because of your brother's accident?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.660
Uh, yeah.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:23.250
Sorry.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.010
It's only been a month.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.120
But you've got to move on eventually.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.530
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:37.640
I feel like this is my only chance to ask, so...

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.640
...do you think you could give me an answer?

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.050
Answer?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.600
You know, I asked if you wanted to go to the Christmas party...

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.510
...together.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.160
Christmas party?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.390
Together...

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:53.360
What?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:57.560
Did you mean, you know...

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:00.640
Yes.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.830
You must be having a hard time.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.920
Sorry for being self-centered.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:18.880
Oh, no...

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.380
You can give me an answer whenever you're ready.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:25.020
Though it would be better if you could tell me before the party.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.810
I'm really sorry!

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.750
An!

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:30.220
You've got it wrong...

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.870
I'm not the one you want.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.720
He's gone.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.230
This isn't my world.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.020
Are you crying?

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:53.660
Shuri-san?

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:57.220
No one's made that mistake before.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.360
Then you're Yukari-san?

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:00.210
Bingo.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.440
Shuri-san...

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:10.410
Are you feeling better?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.990
Yes, thank you.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.290
Good.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.110
Uh...

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.990
Are you the other world's Tomoharu Natsume-kun?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.990
How did you know?

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.360
Nia-chan told me.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:23.270
We're friends.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:26.830
Why did you think I was Shuri?

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:27.940
Oh, I...

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.260
What was the Shuri Kurosaki you know like?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.500
Well...

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.630
There's that sad expression...

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.370
Sorry.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.630
Did something happen?

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.010
Someone I knew died.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:50.650
Many others were hurt.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.470
They must have been very important to you.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:58.080
Everything was fine because they were always there for me.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.730
No matter what.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.460
No matter what happened.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.170
But...

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.130
You loved them.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.510
What should you do now?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.540
Cry?

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:13.770
Despair?

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.150
Neither of those seem correct.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.970
What can you do for the people you love?

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.200
What do you want to do?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.610
I don't want to lose anyone else.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.810
I don't want anyone else to get hurt.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.310
I see.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.780
There you are, Tomoharu.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.470
Take a look at the city.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.230
You should be able to see it.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.750
It's vanishing...

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.070
It's all because of that experiment.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.690
The failure of that experiment tore this world...

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.570
...and now it's being destroyed.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:00.890
But why?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.240
What about the others?

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.970
They can't see it?

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:09.670
The inhabitants of this world don't even realize they're disappearing.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.690
Vanishing erases their very existence.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.570
Their memories will be completely erased.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:20.100
This is the truth...

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:24.920
...and the reason the first Tomoharu was willing to pay any cost...

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.290
...to go to the second world.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:36.280
The tear in this world isn't simply destroying it.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:41.130
Creatures from other worlds pass through the tear into this one.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:48.530
We've got to stop them before they cause any damage.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:52.590
Nia!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.790
It's a monster!

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.080
Get out of here!

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:02.550
The witch of Rakurowa High School...

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.600
Go, quickly!

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:04.570
R-right!

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.280
Let's do this.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.180
There's a lot of them.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.620
What to do...

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.770
This way, everyone!

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.730
Stay calm! Don't panic!

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:20.760
Looks like the student council president is good for something.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:28.920
Saeki!

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.130
Damn you!

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.030
Natsume!

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.200
Shufu, Kurenai, draw!

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.160
Are you alright?

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.510
Y-yes.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.300
Then go. It's not safe here.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:55.300
Yes.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:56.480
Aki-san.

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:58.180
You look okay.

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:00.210
Yes, but...

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.820
We can fix it later...

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:04.140
...as long as we're alive.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.580
We need to get everyone out of here first.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.490
Natsume, get out of here.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:20.540
This way!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.360
Everyone else is fighting...

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.180
...but I'm...

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:28.640
I...

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:34.990
Natsume-kun!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.160
Takatsuki! What...

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:39.570
I was worried about you.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:42.770
Watch out!

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.230
Are you okay, Tomoharu Natsume?

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.020
Aki-san!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:54.820
Aki-san!

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:57.780
It's just a scratch.

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.020
Run, quickly.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.480
I'll do something about this.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:03.160
Aki-san!

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:09.590
I can't...

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.760
I can't protect anyone.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.200
I can't do anything.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:19.990
I don't want this any more!

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:25.870
Natsume-kun, you...

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.190
I made up my mind.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.920
I'm going to protect everyone.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.300
I'm not going to let anyone get hurt!

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.370
Colossus of darkness...

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.280
If this is what it takes...

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.690
...I'll become a demon!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.660
Natsume-kun...

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.360
The friction between worlds...

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.040
...gives humans from other worlds demon powers.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:22.740
Going from the second world to the first had that effect.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:24.260
Yes.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.260
You knew from the start?

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.110
I'm sorry...

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:33.600
I though I could keep you from realizing your powers.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:35.250
But...

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.280
This is the world the first me tried to protect.

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:40.280
It's not my world.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:41.710
I need to go back.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:46.380
Then we'll go to the bridge connecting our worlds.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.110
Yes, but first...

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:52.320
"Nurse's Office"

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:51.790
It's open.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.430
Are you here to visit?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.070
I'm sorry!

00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.900
Sorry for what?

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.900
You hurt yourself protecting me.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.630
It was my decision.

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:06.300
But if I had been able to fight...

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.470
It's in the past now.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:09.120
But...

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.410
Shufu, draw!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.820
Don't worry, I didn't use the blade.

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:16.840
That doesn't mean it didn't hurt.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.520
Once you draw, it's a battle to the death.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:24.190
You need to be prepared...

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.800
...to put your life on the line.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.710
I drew Shufu to protect you.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.000
I have no regrets.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.500
Why would you go so far?

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:39.700
I'm stronger than the average person.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:43.780
I can use that strength to save others.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:46.810
The choice is obvious.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.920
Even if you put yourself in harm's way?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:53.060
Would you let that stop you?

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:55.940
I know you wouldn't.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.120
You have the same look I do.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.910
Aki-san...

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.910
You know, Natsume...

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:03.640
Yes?

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:07.580
I prefer to be thanked rather than apologized to.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.250
Thank you.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.920
That's what I wanted to see.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.860
I'll be going, then.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:17.920
Wait.

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:23.000
You're going to fight an important battle.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:26.170
Take this with you. It's one of my favorites.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.580
Aki-san...

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.220
Thanks for everything.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.620
Tomoharu, there's something I need to tell you.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.940
After being sent here five years ago by Hagane...

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:48.080
...I became involved with a certain research institute.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.760
This is it. La Croix.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.490
I guess it was interesting in its own way.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.570
But a month ago, there was an accident.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:57.660
An accident?

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.720
The superstring gravity reactor...

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:04.770
Yes. Because of that accident, this world is being destroyed.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:08.410
By the time I realized what was going on...

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:09.640
Nia...

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.280
Abandoned by God...

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.780
...humans turned to demons to save their world.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:25.510
Naotaka... the first Tomoharu mentioned that.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:26.390
Yes...

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.060
In order to grant Tomoharu's wish...

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.320
...I made the Asura Machina.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.640
You made the Asura Machina?

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:39.490
Knowing he would die in the second world...

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.190
...I gave him Hagane.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.190
Why?

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:46.130
If he didn't go to the second world...

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.450
...I would never come here.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.330
The Asura Machina never would have been born.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.820
If he didn't go, there would be no way to save this world.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:56.500
Nia-chan.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.580
I had no choice.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:00.790
You don't have to say any more.

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:04.050
No one is blaming you for what you did.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.660
I told him what would happen in the other world!

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:12.360
But he went anyway.

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.950
I couldn't stop him.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:18.180
You loved him.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:19.730
We has kind to me.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:24.020
I was all alone, and he was so kind to me.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.190
It's not your fault, Nia.

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:30.780
Takatsuki and I are grateful to you.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.450
Grateful? Lies...

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.710
It's the truth.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:38.240
Kanade...

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:46.990
You gave us the luck we needed to find each other after what happened, right?

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:50.900
Tomoharu...

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.600
Tomoharu!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.240
What is this?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:05.850
Kurogane!

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:12.580
It's a miracle opening the gravity gate didn't destroy it.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:13.720
Ri-chan!

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:14.660
It's good to see you again.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.100
Or rather, for the first time.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.720
Nice to meet you, Natsume-kun and Kanade.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.210
Ritsu-san, is Kurogane... is Misao alright?

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.420
Why don't you see for yourself?

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.700
Misao-san! But...

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:40.430
She isn't our Misao.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:42.630
She must be...

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:44.570
Bingo!

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:48.890
You're late, Tomo.

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.180
I'll give it to you again.

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:23.360
Someday.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.880
Just a little, okay?

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:27.760
Will the launched memories and remains...

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.760
...laugh like children?

00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:34.980
"Remaining Life, Scattered Life"
